Analysis of the 3 free observations:

- Bf=[1,0,0]→1, Xp=[0,1,0]→0, Zn=[1,1,0]→0

Testing all ±p_i OP ±p_j formulas against these three points, four survive:
- H1: (p0 AND ¬p1)
- H2: (¬p1 OR p2)
- H3: (¬p1 XOR p2)  [≡ p1 XNOR p2]
- H5: (¬p1 AND ¬p2)

(pair (p0,p2) is fully eliminated — no sign/OP combo fits all three).

Checking untested symbols, Nd=[1,0,1] predicts: H1=1, H2=1, H3=0, H5=0 — a clean 2-2 split. Following up with Wt=[0,1,1] (H1=0,H2=1,H3=1,H5=0) would then fully disambiguate all four regardless of Nd's result. So committing to TEST(Nd) first.

